  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "text": "One day without it would expose satellites and power grids to more charged particles; the atmosphere would not vanish in a day.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "NOAA",
      "role": "consequence"
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "text": "Assume earth's magnetic field switched off for one day.",
      "class": "SPECULATION",
      "layer": "SPECULATIVE SCENARIO",
      "source": "NOAA",
      "role": "trigger"
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "text": "The governing physics: the geodynamo in Earth's liquid outer core generates a field that deflects the solar wind.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "NOAA",
      "role": "mechanism"
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "text": "The key figure: 780,000 years.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "NOAA",
      "role": "number"
    },
    {
      "id": "C5",
      "text": "Losing the field for a day would not strip the atmosphere; that takes far longer.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "NOAA",
      "role": "misconception"
    },
    {
      "id": "C6",
      "text": "Earth's magnetic field is already weakening.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C7",
      "text": "Its main dipole has faded about 6.3% per century.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C8",
      "text": "Fields have flipped 183 times in 83 million years.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C9",
      "text": "The last flip was 780,000 years ago.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C10",
      "text": "Now switch it off completely, for just one day.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C11",
      "text": "Satellites and power grids would take more charged particles.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C12",
      "text": "But the air wouldn't vanish in a day; that takes far longer.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C13",
      "text": "So we'd survive, but our technology would feel it first.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "editorial narration (case file)",
      "role": "narration"
    },
    {
      "id": "C14",
      "text": "Over the last two centuries the dipole strength has been decreasing at a rate of about 6.3% per century.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "KNOWN SCIENCE",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Earth's magnetic field",
      "role": "evidence"
    },
    {
      "id": "C15",
      "text": "Measurements since Gauss in 1832 show a relative decay of about 10% over the last 150 years.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "KNOWN SCIENCE",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Earth's magnetic field",
      "role": "evidence"
    },
    {
      "id": "C16",
      "text": "There have been at least 183 reversals over the last 83 million years, on average once every ~450,000 years.",
